# Exp 7 — landing vocabulary: exp_fin and quest_fin

## TL;DR

Owner-coined terms (2026-11-15). Today "land" names
three different merges (exp edge, quest branch merge,
promotion to master) and only the first is a real FSM
move. Two finish lines get their own words:

- `exp_fin` — an experiment has landed (its `land` edge
  taken, state `landed`). The exp-level finish line.
- `quest_fin` — the quest is done and merging back to
  master (promotion). The quest-level finish line, and
  the only owner-gated one.

## Diagram

```text
todo -> ... -> approved --land edge--> landed   == exp_fin
quest branch --quest_fin (owner gate, demo first)--> master
```

## Pseudocode

```python
def report(exp):  return "exp_fin"   if exp.state == "landed"
def report(quest): return "quest_fin" if quest.promoted_to_master
# land stays the edge name; fin words name the finish lines, not new edges
```

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Intent | one word per finish line; promotion stops borrowing the exp verb |
| Lane | standard (skill change; own exp per rule 6.6) |
| Output | the terms propagated everywhere the finish lines are named: `skills/induct/SKILL.md`, the induct workflows' return vocabulary, `bp3 q` report/rollup presentation in `src/`, tests naming the finish lines, QUEST.md terms sync; installed copies. FSM state spelling `landed` in code/data does not change — `exp_fin`/`quest_fin` are the report words the codebase speaks at the two finish lines |
| Depends on | Exp 3, Exp 6 (report language rides the conductor rewrite) |

## Acceptance (fails today: reports say only landed/landed)

| Case | Expected |
|---|---|
| exp reaches landed | conductor report and workflow outcomes name it `exp_fin` (state itself stays `landed`) |
| quest promotion to master completes | the promotion report names it `quest_fin` |
| term sync | `exp_fin` / `quest_fin` spelled identically in skill text, workflow returns, `src/` report strings, tests, and QUEST.md; no synonym (promoted, merged, done) names either finish line; `landed` remains the FSM state in data |
| no new edges | bp3 q gains no fin edges; these are report/term words, not state |

## Acceptance test (goal block)

- **Objective:** you can tell which finish line a
  report is about without context.
- **Prove by:** grep the installed skills and workflow
  returns for both terms; this quest's own landing
  report uses `quest_fin`.
- **Done when:** both terms are live in the conductor's
  vocabulary and used in this quest's reports.

## Tests

known cases: the Acceptance table · property-based:
none — term sync is a finite grep check (stated
omission) · fixtures: skills tests · demos: Demo
trace, observed at landing.

## Context

Owner, 2026-11-15: "why do we land on master
immediately? land means we first merge back to the
quest itself; the real land is from the quest to
master." The red-chair pass found the word doing three
jobs with the least machinery on the biggest one.
`exp_fin` / `quest_fin` split the finish lines so the
owner gate can attach to exactly one word: `quest_fin`.
